    "body": "Ultimately I think this decision belongs in the hands of those who contribute the most; being able to easily edit HTML is more important than any such auxiliary tooling considerations.\r\n\r\nAs one of those people, I'm not interested in splitting as I find a single file much easier to edit and deal with the history of. The single-file workflow is also what every other spec I work with does.\r\n\r\nFinally, I'll note that the \"pages\" of the multipage edition are an artifact that change over time and not something stable that can be relied on. See all the various redirects we've added over time as they change. https://github.com/whatwg/misc-server/blob/main/debian/marquee/nginx/sites/html.spec.whatwg.org.conf#L14",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
