    "created_at": "2023-09-06T10:18:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-06T10:18:02Z",
    "body": "> I am currently working on an HTML parser implementation and I'd like to be able to:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> $ git diff $SOME_COMMIT src/parsing \r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> to see all the changes to the [parsing page](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html) since `$SOME_COMMIT`. But alas I currently can only diff the `source` file without being able to filter out what I don't care about.\r\n\r\nThe following will show a log of all commits that changed any part of the _“Parsing HTML documents”_ section:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngit log -L\"/Parsing HTML documents<\\/h3>/,/Serializing HTML fragments<\\/h3>/:source\" --no-patch\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe [`-L` option](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-log#Documentation/git-log.txt--Lltstartgtltendgtltfilegt) is useful in general for tracking changes to specific parts of files (and not even just for long files).\r\n\r\nThe [`--since` option](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-log#Documentation/git-log.txt---sinceltdategt) can be added to show only commits since a particular date (e.g., the date of a particular commit).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
