    "body": "@sideshowbarker Thanks, I didn't know about `-L`. However that command seems to be really slow and a list of commits isn't really reviewable (compared to a diff).\r\n\r\n> in theory any normative change has a corresponding web-platform-tests PR as well as bugs filed against implementers\r\n\r\nI see that you folks generally use \"implementers\" to refer to browser vendors that implement all of the specification. I was using the term in a more general sense to also include developers of e.g. HTML parser libraries that only implement a subset of the spec. web-platform-tests appears to be a test suite for browsers, which again wouldn't really be helpful for a library implementing only a part of the spec as far as I can tell.\r\n\r\nAnyways I wrote a small Python script to address the lack of section-wise diffability: #9700 ... it would be nice if it could be included in the repository for the benefit of others. Cheers!",
